It became NaN within frames. Only camera.update changes yaw. So inputLook.x or sensitivity causing. Current look 0 at end. But maybe `lookX` is undefined because `this.input.update()` returns properties? It returns `{ lookX, lookY, zoom }`; fine.

Wait UI constructor calls `_bindSettings`:
```
music.addEventListener('input', () => { g.settings.music = +music.value; ...});
...
```
No.

Camera update:
```
if (!this.freeze) {
 if (inputLook) {
   this.yaw -= inputLook.x * 0.0042 * this.sensitivity;
   this.pitch += inputLook.y *...
...
```
`inputLook` object `{lookX, lookY, zoom}` has x undefined! Because Input.update returns lookX/lookY, but camera expects x/y. That's it! `inputLook.x` undefined → yaw NaN. Fix camera.js to accept x/y or lookX/lookY. Best change:
```
const lx = inputLook.x ?? inputLook.lookX ?? 0;
const ly = inputLook.y ?? inputLook.lookY ?? 0;
const z = inputLook.zoom ?? 0;
```
Also zoom. Great.

