Now add segment-AABB function and use. After raycast block, before pos. Need the ray origin `from`, direction `dirNormalized`, length. We can add helper outside class.

Implementation:
```
function rayBoxHit(origin, dir, box, maxDist) {
  let tmin = 0.0001, tmax = maxDist;
  const axes = [['x','minX','maxX'],...];
  for (...) {
    const o=origin[axis], d=dir[axis], lo=box[min], hi=box[max];
    if (Math.abs(d)<1e-6) { if (o<lo||o>hi) return null; }
    else { let t1=(lo-o)/d, t2=(hi-o)/d; if(t1>t2)[t1,t2]=[t2,t1]; tmin=Math.max(tmin,t1); tmax=Math.min(tmax,t2); if(tmin>tmax) return null; }
  }
  return tmin;
}
```
Within update, compute dir before; use `from` and `rayDir` normalized. For each box, if focus inside box (slab tmin=0 with origin inside), skip. We can test containment:
```
if (from.x>minX && ... && from.y>... ) continue;
```
Then hit distance; minDist. Use hit - 0.15 but >= minDistance. We already clamp final.
But if a hit is at 0.4 and minDistance 0.55, still inside. We can set minDistance 0.45, camera near 0.06 so okay. But camera can end up inside cat. Use 0.5. Better use max(0.35, hit -0.15). Could temporarily pull closer than minDistance when needed. Set `dist = Math.min(dist, Math.max(0.4, hit - 0.15))`. Good.

